course: dictionary
lesson: 9574
title: One word, many meanings: strap
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A strap is a strip of leather, cloth or plastic. Its job is to hold things together or in place. When you meet «strap» in a text, read the words around it to find out which meaning the writer means. «A helmet fits snug and level, just above the eyebrows, with the strap buckled» tells you the strap holds the helmet on your head.
explain: Strap can also be a verb, a doing word. «Before the ride, Sam had to strap his bag on tight» shows that to strap something means to fasten it with a strap. The word «buckled» is a clue here, because a buckle is what fastens a strap.
explain: Some uses are more surprising. «The nurse will strap up his sore ankle» means she will wrap it with a bandage, and the word «ankle» tells you it is an injury. Another phrase is «strapped for cash», which means having very little money. The words «for cash» give the clue, because cash is money.
explain: Always check the meaning by putting it into the sentence. If you read «The helmet strap holds the helmet» and it makes sense, you have the right meaning. If it does not, look at the other words around it, then try again.
fact: A strap is a strip of leather, cloth or plastic.
fact: «Strap» can be a noun (a thing) or a verb (a doing word): «a strap», «to strap».
fact: To strap something is to fasten it with a strap, as in «strap in» or «strap your bag on».
fact: «Strap up» means wrap an injury with a bandage.
fact: «Strapped for cash» is an informal phrase meaning having very little money.
exercise: «A helmet fits snug and level, just above the eyebrows, with the strap buckled.» What does the buckled strap do? | It cools your head | It stops the helmet from getting wet | *It holds the helmet firmly in place | It makes the helmet heavier
exercise: «Before the ride, Sam had to strap his bag on tight.» What does strap mean here? | *To fasten with a strap | To wash thoroughly | To cut into small pieces | To paint in bright colours
exercise: Jayden says, «We're strapped for cash this month.» What does strapped for cash mean? | Losing a purse on the bus | Tied up with a rope | Holding a lot of money in a bag | *Having very little money
test: «The nurse will strap up his sore ankle.» What does strap up mean? | *To wrap with a bandage | To cut the ankle open | To walk on it carefully | To take the bandage off
test: Why does a seat belt have straps? | *To hold you in place for safety | To carry shopping | To make the seat softer | To decorate the car
exam: «When you get off, make sure bag straps do not catch on the handrail.» Which word best describes a bag strap? | A loud noise | A pocket inside the bag | *A strip used to fasten or carry something | A small animal
